00:01:27.884 --> 00:01:33.626
<v Daniel>journal PNAS by Julian Berger and his colleagues at the Max Planck Institute for Human Development.</v>

11
00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:46.199
<v Maya>OK, let's unpack this, because before we can really appreciate the massive breakthrough in this 2026 Berger paper, We have to establish the rather depressing baseline that the scientific community had, you know, basically just accepted as a fact of life.</v>

12
00:01:46.339 --> 00:02:01.026
<v Daniel>Yeah, we really need to talk about the AI penalty. To set the stage, we have to look back at a major 2024 meta-analysis. This was published in Nature Human Behavior by Vaccaro, Almatuk, and Malone. They wanted to survey the entire landscape of human-AI collaboration.</v>

13
00:02:01.446 --> 00:02:16.409
<v Daniel>So they analyzed 74 different studies. I mean, we are talking about 370 distinct effect sizes. Wow. Which basically means 370 specific test scenarios across all sorts of tasks, everything from predicting house</v>

14
