00:10:41.946 --> 00:10:42.226
<v Daniel>present.</v>

84
00:10:42.266 --> 00:10:48.189
<v Maya>That feels like a massive victory for human potential. I mean, we aren't broken. We just need the right environment to learn.</v>

85
00:10:48.269 --> 00:10:48.990
<v Daniel>Yeah, exactly.</v>

86
00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:59.394
<v Maya>But and I'm guessing here I have a feeling the story doesn't wrap up neatly with a bow right here. Does feedback perfectly fix this charismatic AI problem every time?</v>

87
00:10:59.574 --> 00:11:13.237
<v Daniel>No, it doesn't. And this raises a critical tension in the literature. It brings us to a 2021 study by Bansal and colleagues called Does the Hole Exceed Its Parts? Now, this study is actually one of the rare 10 studies from the meta analysis that did provide feedback.</v>

