00:11:27.089 --> 00:11:28.350
<v Maya>Oh, LSAT questions. Okay.</v>

91
00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:41.196
<v Daniel>Right. And even with feedback available, they found that giving humans AI explanations mostly just made people blindly accept the AI's advice. It increased their reliance on the AI regardless of whether the AI was actually right or wrong.</v>

92
00:11:41.747 --> 00:11:50.213
<v Maya>Wait, why do we do this? Even when we are being shown that the AI gets things wrong sometimes, why do our brains just default to trusting a well-written paragraph?</v>

93
00:11:50.513 --> 00:11:56.798
<v Daniel>It comes down to a psychological phenomenon, often called automation bias, combined with cognitive offloading.</v>

94
00:11:56.878 --> 00:11:58.059
